{
  "description": "A node's own knobly text (docs/control-port.md#a-nodes-own-text), the feature node-text, over a file with a snippet that makes a node (t1) and a comment owned by rec's statement. graphFile.subscribe's GraphFile carries nodeTexts: where each node's statement is in its text, owned comments included, t1's in its snippet and shared. In order: node.setText replacing rec's statement (graphFile.changed cause edit with the new text and nodeTexts, node.updated, then the reply); the same version again (file-changed); a text whose setting is given twice (invalid-text, the diagnostic placed in the text sent); a text naming another node (ear/node-renamed at the name); t1, whose statement is a snippet's (shared-definition at it); two statements (ear/not-one-node). Then node.addText appending rec2 with its comment (graphFile.changed with rec2's nodeTexts, node.added, the reply); a stale version (file-changed); a { closed on the wrong line (knobly's E2001, placed in the text); two statements (ear/not-one-node); a name already taken (the graph's duplicate-node). file is the graph file the client holds at the end, graph the graph.",
